today is dr martin luther king jr day  normally there will be events held all  across the valley including the annual  parade downtown but  the pandemic has changed those plans  still people have found ways to honor  the  memory of the civil rights leader bianca  holman live this afternoon in the  historic west side of las vegas with the  story today bianca  this day might be a day off for some or  a moment to post  a quote on social media but for people  here at the vegas  community garden it was a day of action  to honor martin luther king jr it was a  call to service  and to serve the community the pandemic  impacted many traditional mlk events  but here at the vegas roots community  garden people planted healing herbs like  lavender thyme and cilantro  they were still able to participate in  the national day of service  the first planting is for health care  workers who serve  working-class communities of color in  north las vegas  the plots were also named after longtime  community activist  rudy duncan we've got a wide range of  people from a wide variety of  backgrounds  the diversity and the coming together  and i think that food  and gardening is the one thing that  unites us all so it's very important for  us to do an herb garden with  healing properties because we feel that  miss ruby has  encouraged and healed the community  throughout her decades of service  ruby duncan led 6 000 people in a march  for poor people's rights down las vegas  strip in the 70s  she was also instrumental in bringing  resources to nevada's black and working  poor communities  now the goal of the vegas roots  community garden is to nourish the  community  just like miss duncan did for decades  and also this community garden is open  to everyone  and they even have fresh produce for  purchase reporting from near tonopah and  bonanza  bianca holman 8 news now
 

